astrocam v3 units are NOT ansible-managed — they won't survive a reimage.

From astro-polecam, 2026-08-13. STATE.md:315 has flagged this for a while;
raising it now because cover automation just landed on top of the unmanaged
pieces, so a reimage would now lose working behaviour, not just config.

Installed BY HAND on astrocam (root-owned, not in ansible):
  - astrocam-v3-night.service
  - astrocam-v3-uploader.service
  - astrocam-v3-gate.service + astrocam-v3-gate.timer
  - /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/50-astrocam.rules
    (lets peter toggle the services without sudo; the gate needs this)

Repo copies of the gate SCRIPT and the polkit rule are committed under
~/astro/astrocam/, but the systemd unit files and the INSTALLED polkit rule
are not managed. eclipticam's equivalents ARE ansible-managed, so there's a
working pattern to copy — likely just extending that role to astrocam.

New since 2026-08-13: the gate now also drives the lens cover (opens before
the night daemon starts, closes after it stops), persisting position in
/var/lib/astrocam/cover.json. astrocam commit 002d0a6, not yet pushed. So
"reimage loses the gate" now also means "reimage loses cover automation and
the lens sits open all day".

Not urgent, no deadline — but it's the last hand-installed corner of an
otherwise-automated camera.
